{:mulog/duration 573625, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.command-processor-v2.core", :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace nil, :ai.obney.grain.command-processor-v2.core/command {:tick-id #uuid "df4bf3e3-32e9-4394-a65f-5ddbcfc013bd", :node-path [{:type :leaf, :node-id #uuid "a76b7c99-445a-4f85-b297-26490cab89c4"}], :command/name :sheet/record-rlm-tree-node-completion, :command/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T21:03:14.581668-05:00", :command/id #uuid "ac3a9417-5ffe-48f2-a1ee-54e3894ed63d", :usage {:prompt-tokens 26515, :completion-tokens 736, :total-tokens 27251}, :node-id #uuid "a76b7c99-445a-4f85-b297-26490cab89c4", :input-profile {:contract_v2 {:type :string, :length 55944, :word-count 8763, :line-count 900}, :contract_v3 {:type :string, :length 48885, :word-count 7568, :line-count 802}, :section-diffs {:type :string, :length 3947, :word-count 548, :line-count 41}}, :sheet-id #uuid "9077987c-1f87-41e8-af6c-ee2b9b1ff3c4"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YhcC7p330DuzyOrq9_FWqir2tcE0k", :mulog/timestamp 1779242594581, :metric/name "CommandProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YhcC7p330DuzyOrq9_FWqir2tcE0k", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.command-processor-v2.core/process-command, :metric/resolution :high}
{:mulog/parent-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YhcBLetZYlJXh5GoVD6unWtEBGg8_", :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YhcBLetZYlJXh5GoVD6unWtEBGg8_", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YhcCg8BXqfL-TTfXy2cq8_v3UPjv-", :mulog/timestamp 1779242594584, :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/anomaly-in-todo-processor, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :anomaly {:cognitect.anomalies/category :cognitect.anomalies/fault, :cognitect.anomalies/message "Todo Processor returned nil: %s"}}
{:mulog/duration 5606750, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace nil, :event {:tick-id #uuid "df4bf3e3-32e9-4394-a65f-5ddbcfc013bd", :writes {:major-changes "Based on the provided section-diffs and contract texts, the major changes are as follows:\n\n1.  **Elimination of Domestic Content Requirements**: \n    - The most significant change is the complete removal of all \"Domestic Content\" mandates. In v2.0, Solar PV projects were required to maintain a 60% domestic content level, supported by detailed grids and reporting requirements (Appendix C). In v3.1.1, these sections, definitions, and representations (Section 4.4.4) have been entirely deleted.\n\n2.  **Implementation of \"Prescribed Forms\" for Contract Actions**:\n    - v3.1.1 introduces a requirement that key administrative actions—including change of contact info (Section 7.2), supplier termination (Section 8.1), and contract amendments (Section 9)—must now be executed using a \"Prescribed Form\" found on the OPA website. v2.0 allowed for more general written notice.\n\n3.  **Expanded Information Disclosure for Public Safety**:\n    - Section 6.5 has been updated to grant the OPA authority to disclose facility and supplier information to government agencies and emergency services for \"public health and safety\" and \"emergency response\" planning.\n\n4.  **Discretionary Eligibility and Building Classification**:\n    - Appendix A (\"Project Eligibility Requirements\") and Appendix C (\"Existing Building\") were modified to grant the OPA \"sole and absolute discretion\" to grant exceptions for previously contracted facilities or to deem certain structures as \"Existing Buildings\" for Rooftop Facility classification.", :impact-analysis "For each major change, the shift in risk and benefit is analyzed below:\n\n1.  **Elimination of Domestic Content Requirements**:\n    - **Shift**: Significant benefit to the **Supplier**.\n    - **Analysis**: This removes a substantial compliance burden and legal risk. Under v2.0, failing to meet the 60% threshold was a breach of warranty. Suppliers now have greater flexibility in sourcing equipment (e.g., inverters, modules) from global markets rather than being restricted to Ontario-based manufacturers.\n\n2.  **Requirement of \"Prescribed Forms\"**:\n    - **Shift**: Benefit to the **OPA**.\n    - **Analysis**: This streamlines OPA administration but increases the procedural burden on the **Supplier**. If a supplier provides notice of termination or change of address in a standard letter rather than the OPA’s specific \"Prescribed Form,\" the OPA could technically deem the notice invalid.\n\n3.  **Expanded Information Disclosure**:\n    - **Shift**: Benefit to the **OPA/Public Authority**; Risk to the **Supplier**.\n    - **Analysis**: This broadens the scope of how the Supplier's data is used. While it serves a public safety purpose, it slightly reduces the Supplier's privacy protections regarding facility data and location.\n\n4.  **Discretionary Eligibility and Building Classification**:\n    - **Shift**: Benefit to the **OPA**.\n    - **Analysis**: By adding \"sole and absolute discretion\" language, the OPA gains the power to act as the final arbiter on eligibility disputes without being strictly bound by the definitions. While this allows for flexibility that *could* benefit a Supplier (e.g., getting a project approved that otherwise wouldn't fit), the legal weight gives the OPA total control over the interpretation, making it harder for Suppliers to challenge OPA decisions in court or arbitration."}, :duration-ms 5960, :event/tags #{[:sheet #uuid "9077987c-1f87-41e8-af6c-ee2b9b1ff3c4"] [:node #uuid "a76b7c99-445a-4f85-b297-26490cab89c4"] [:tick #uuid "df4bf3e3-32e9-4394-a65f-5ddbcfc013bd"]}, :event/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T21:03:14.576092-05:00", :usage {:prompt-tokens 26515, :completion-tokens 736, :total-tokens 27251}, :status :success, :node-id #uuid "a76b7c99-445a-4f85-b297-26490cab89c4", :event/type :sheet/node-execution-completed, :sheet-id #uuid "9077987c-1f87-41e8-af6c-ee2b9b1ff3c4", :event/id #uuid "019e431f-7110-7095-b261-4d155af4ac08"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YhcBLetZYlJXh5GoVD6unWtEBGg8_", :mulog/timestamp 1779242594578, :metric/name "TodoProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YhcBLetZYlJXh5GoVD6unWtEBGg8_", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/processing-event, :metric/resolution :high}
